FreeType 2.14 added diacritic handling to its autohinter. A database of
characters with diacritics drives tilde stretching, blue zone exclusions
and a pass that separates diacritics from their bases, and a new check in
af_latin_hint_edges rejects a serif with other edges between it and its
stem. skrifa deliberately has neither, so this turns both off: the
database lookup finds nothing, and the serif check never runs.

